`md list` prints an ABSOLUTE path in every record, and the harness runs each
case in a scratch directory whose name is random, so a line holding a path can
never be pinned byte for byte. Cases that list at least one file therefore pipe
the output through `md lines`, which selects the lines that hold no path.

--format toml re-serializes YAML frontmatter as TOML. One string key is one
`key = value` line.

The value is quoted with SINGLE quotes, a TOML literal string. This case first
asserted double quotes, and that expectation was wrong rather than the tool:
TOML gives both spellings, they parse to the same value, and the emitter is free
to pick either. A literal string carries no escapes, so the choice only shows on
a value holding a quote or a backslash, which this one does not.
